<!-- =====================================================
     PHASE 9 BANNER
     ===================================================== -->
<div class="p9-banner">
    <div class="p9-phase-pill">Phase 9 · Self-Sustaining Steam Dynamo</div>
    <h1>Water-Only <em>Self-Sustaining Steam Dynamo</em></h1>
    <p>
        Phase 9 removes the grid charge port and solar panels entirely. Six upgraded 200A  48V
        generators — driven by the steam pistons — feed a supercapacitor buffer bank, a carbon-fibre
        flywheel energy store, and a thermoelectric generator (TEG) array on the condenser.
        Combined output targets enough electrical surplus to keep the 40 kWh pack topped without
        ever plugging in. Fuel: distilled water and maintenance only.
    </p>
</div>

<!-- =====================================================
     PHASE 9 HEADLINE METRICS
     ===================================================== -->
<div class="p9-section">

    <div class="p9-section-label">Phase 9 · Complete System Specification</div>
    <h2 class="p9-section-title">6 × 200A generators · supercap buffer · flywheel · TEG waste recovery</h2>
    <p class="p9-section-lead">
        The self-sustaining loop works by recovering energy at every stage of the steam cycle.
        Generators extract electrical energy from piston rotation. The supercapacitor bank
        absorbs regen spikes that would otherwise damage the lithium pack. The flywheel stores
        surplus rotational energy during light-load phases and releases it during demand spikes.
        The TEG array harvests the thermal differential across the condenser — energy that Phase 8
        threw away as heat. Net result: the 40 kWh pack stays above 80% SOC indefinitely under
        normal driving conditions. The system needs no plug, no sun. Only water.
    </p>

