            <ul class="p9-spec-list">
                <li><strong>Principle: Seebeck effect — ΔT between steam exhaust and ambient</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Hot side: Condenser face ~120°C (exhaust steam)</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Cold side: Ambient air ~30°C (forced convection)</strong></li>
                <li><strong>ΔT: ~90°C → 5–8% conversion efficiency</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Output range: 500W (partial load) to 2,000W (full steam)</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Cell type: Bi₂Te₃ thermoelectric modules — automotive grade</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Mounting: Sandwiched on condenser hot face — passive installation</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Energy was: Previously wasted to atmosphere in Phase 8</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Maintenance: Zero moving parts — solid state, no wear</strong></li>
            </ul>
